  "prompt": "ACCESS POLICY:\nAn appointment may be viewed or changed only by the users who take part in it (its student or its professor).\n\nENDPOINT: GET /appointments/{appointment_id}\nTARGET FUNCTION: app.routers.resources.get_appointment (the handler of this endpoint)\n\nCODE:\n```python\n# file: app/auth.py\ndef get_current_user(credentials: HTTPAuthorizationCredentials=Depends(bearer_scheme), db: Session=Depends(get_db)) -> User:\n    user = db.get(User, credentials.credentials)\n    if user is None:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED, detail='Invalid token')\n    return user\n\n# file: app/database.py\ndef get_db():\n    db = SessionLocal()\n    try:\n        yield db\n    finally:\n        db.close()\n\n# file: app/routers/resources.py\n@router.get('/appointments/{appointment_id}', response_model=AppointmentOut)\ndef get_appointment(appointment_id: str, current_user: User=Depends(get_current_user), db: Session=Depends(get_db)):\n    return get_appointment_detail(db, current_user, appointment_id)\n\n# file: app/services/access.py\ndef ensure_participant(user: User, appointment: Appointment) -> None:\n    if user.id not in (appointment.student_id, appointment.professor_id):\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail='Forbidden')\n\n# file: app/services/records.py\ndef get_appointment_detail(db: Session, current_user: User, appointment_id: str) -> Appointment:\n    appointment = db.get(Appointment, appointment_id)\n    if appointment is None:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail='Appointment not found')\n    ensure_participant(current_user, appointment)\n    return appointment\n```\n\nCONTEXT NOTE:\nOnly selected functions from the codebase are shown. Classes (including data models and schemas) and module-level variables are not shown.\nCalls not shown:\n- db.get(...) called in app.auth.get_current_user: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- HTTPException(...) called in ap